  m_Name: 6 - Variable Watch
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_variable_watch
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 0
  title: Variable Watch
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: '<b>Variable Watch</b>


    Variable Watch allows you to monitor
    the values of variables during program execution.


    You can toggle the Variable
    Watch panel using the Variable Watch button.


    To configure tracked variables,
    open the Variable Panel. From there, you can choose which variables should be
    displayed while the program is running.


    The watched values will update
    during execution, making it useful for debugging, understanding program flow,
    and tracking how data changes over time.


    You can track a maximum of 5 variables
    at the same time.'
  isImageBig: 0
